          "title": "You'll want to know: फटना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फटना — phaṭnā — \"to tear, to burst\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फटना (phaṭnā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from sphāṭayati, \"causes to split\" (CDIAL 13825). phaṭnā is the self-acting form, with the short vowel such verbs take."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
